# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / heavyweight data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/raw holds the downloaded OSM extract plus the OSRM .osrm* graph build
# artefacts (hundreds of MB); both are reproduced by `npm run osrm:init`.
# data/processed holds grid.parquet / samples.parquet from `npm run data`.
# The directory scaffolding is kept with .gitkeep so the quickstart curl/scripts
# have somewhere to write.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (uv)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# S2 experiment scratch (generated by experiments/build_s2_graph.py + pll)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
experiments/s2_graph.npz
experiments/s2_graph.bin
experiments/*.labels
experiments/pll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Container / runtime scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors & OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTE: the exported models (server/models/model.onnx and the compiled
# server/models/model.bin) and the benchmark fixture (tests/golden_routes.json)
# are intentionally tracked. They let a fresh clone run the service and the test
# suite without re-running OSRM. model.bin is a deterministic re-serialisation of
# model.onnx: `uv run python/export_binary.py`.
